1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,745
I wake up at 3:45 in the morning.

2
00:00:04,745 --> 00:00:07,886
Everyone thinks I'm crazy.

3
00:00:07,886 --> 00:00:14,020
But I smile before I open my eyes.

4
00:07:56,097 --> 00:08:00,072
I wake up at 3:45 in the morning.

5
00:08:00,072 --> 00:08:03,897
Yes, 3:45.

6
00:08:03,897 --> 00:08:07,110
Everyone thinks I'm crazy.

7
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:09,892
Maybe they are right.

8
00:08:09,892 --> 00:08:14,163
But I smile before I open my eyes.

9
00:08:14,163 --> 00:08:21,777
Because today, like every day, I am going to do the thing I love most.

10
00:08:23,077 --> 00:08:31,013
My name is Marcos. I am 38 years old. And I'm a baker.

11
00:08:31,013 --> 00:08:35,941
It's my job, and it's my passion.

12
00:08:35,941 --> 00:08:40,991
I would never have thought to say it at twenty years old.

13
00:08:40,991 --> 00:08:44,667
But that's how it is.

14
00:08:45,967 --> 00:08:54,814
I get dressed in silence so as not to wake up my wife Ana and little Sofía.

15
00:08:54,814 --> 00:09:00,207
A white t-shirt, comfortable pants.

16
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:06,687
I kiss my wife on the cheek. She sleeps.

17
00:09:06,687 --> 00:09:11,647
He smiles at me without opening his eyes.

18
00:09:12,947 --> 00:09:15,188
I leave home.

19
00:09:15,188 --> 00:09:20,237
The streets of the town are empty.

20
00:09:20,237 --> 00:09:27,186
Just me, the full moon, and some curious cat.

21
00:09:27,186 --> 00:09:30,686
I walk to the bakery.

22
00:09:30,686 --> 00:09:35,566
It's just a five-minute walk.

23
00:09:36,866 --> 00:09:40,086
I open the door to my bakery.

24
00:09:40,086 --> 00:09:44,628
The smell greets me immediately.

25
00:09:44,628 --> 00:09:51,615
Flour, yeast, old wood.

26
00:09:51,615 --> 00:09:56,826
For others it will be a strange smell.

27
00:09:56,826 --> 00:10:02,546
For me it is the perfume of happiness.

28
00:10:03,846 --> 00:10:06,586
I turn on the lights.

29
00:10:06,586 --> 00:10:10,106
I put on the white apron.

30
00:10:10,106 --> 00:10:13,446
I open the bag of flour.

31
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:18,070
Hands sink into the soft flour.

32
00:10:18,070 --> 00:10:20,786
It's cold.

33
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:24,706
The magic begins.

34
00:10:26,006 --> 00:10:29,427
I work the dough by hand.

35
00:10:29,427 --> 00:10:35,833
Fast. Strong. Almost a dance.

36
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:42,986
My father taught me this way, and his father before him.

37
00:10:42,986 --> 00:10:49,146
Three generations of hands in this same flour.

38
00:10:50,446 --> 00:10:54,523
I put the loaves in the old oven.

39
00:10:54,523 --> 00:11:00,326
I look at him. The fire makes noise inside.

40
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:05,626
The bread begins to rise slowly.

41
00:11:05,626 --> 00:11:13,346
This moment, every day, excites me a little.

42
00:11:14,656 --> 00:11:18,496
At 5:30 the first bread is ready.

43
00:11:18,496 --> 00:11:24,997
The bakery is filled with the best perfume in the world.

44
00:11:24,997 --> 00:11:27,906
I open the door.

45
00:11:27,906 --> 00:11:32,806
The day begins for the people.

46
00:11:34,107 --> 00:11:42,680
The first client is always Mrs. Lina. He is 80 years old.

47
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:47,301
Buy half a loaf and two buns.

48
00:11:47,301 --> 00:11:51,667
Every day. He tells me:

49
00:11:51,667 --> 00:11:56,534
"Marcos, you are as good as your father."

50
00:11:56,534 --> 00:11:58,007
I smile.

51
00:11:58,007 --> 00:12:02,037
I feel proud.

52
00:12:03,337 --> 00:12:06,277
Then the workers arrive.

53
00:12:06,277 --> 00:12:10,421
Then the mothers with the children.

54
00:12:10,421 --> 00:12:15,795
Then the employees running to work.

55
00:12:15,795 --> 00:12:20,042
Everyone greets me by name.

56
00:12:20,042 --> 00:12:23,539
I know their names.

57
00:12:23,539 --> 00:12:28,307
It's like a big family.

58
00:12:29,607 --> 00:12:35,570
One day a little boy walks in, alone for the first time.

59
00:12:35,570 --> 00:12:38,327
He is six years old.

60
00:12:38,327 --> 00:12:41,582
He looks at me with fear.

61
00:12:41,582 --> 00:12:46,446
He has a one euro coin in his hand.

62
00:12:46,446 --> 00:12:48,857
Whispers:

63
00:12:48,857 --> 00:12:53,647
"I would like… a small loaf of bread, please."

64
00:12:53,647 --> 00:12:58,687
I give him a hot, freshly baked roll.

65
00:12:58,687 --> 00:13:03,527
"It's a gift. For your first time alone."

66
00:13:03,527 --> 00:13:06,137
His eyes light up.

67
00:13:06,137 --> 00:13:10,987
He runs away, happy.

68
00:13:12,286 --> 00:13:15,926
Around midday the problem arrives.

69
00:13:15,926 --> 00:13:19,180
The oven makes a strange noise.

70
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:22,306
I look at him worried.

71
00:13:22,306 --> 00:13:24,886
I try to fix it.

72
00:13:24,886 --> 00:13:28,864
The oven is old, like me.

73
00:13:28,864 --> 00:13:31,126
I caress him.

74
00:13:31,126 --> 00:13:37,246
It seems silly, I know. But then it works again.

75
00:13:37,246 --> 00:13:42,414
Maybe he wasn't that stupid.

76
00:13:43,716 --> 00:13:48,316
At two in the afternoon I close the bakery.

77
00:13:48,316 --> 00:13:52,696
I return home tired but happy.

78
00:13:52,696 --> 00:13:59,736
As I walk, I see the others starting their lunch break.

79
00:13:59,736 --> 00:14:04,536
My work day is already over.

80
00:14:04,536 --> 00:14:09,396
They just started theirs.

81
00:14:10,696 --> 00:14:14,623
At home my wife has prepared the pasta.

82
00:14:14,623 --> 00:14:18,177
Sofia jumps on me.

83
00:14:18,177 --> 00:14:23,313
"Dad, you're back! You smell like bread!"

84
00:14:23,313 --> 00:14:27,030
I hug her tight.

85
00:14:27,030 --> 00:14:31,340
We eat together, the three of us.

86
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:34,900
Then I sleep for two hours.

87
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:39,168
A well-deserved nap.

88
00:14:48,365 --> 00:14:54,855
Aren't you tired? Wouldn't you like to sleep in?"

89
00:14:54,855 --> 00:14:59,062
I always respond the same way.

90
00:14:59,062 --> 00:15:05,285
"Yes, I'm tired. But I'm happy.

91
00:15:05,285 --> 00:15:08,045
And do you know one thing?

92
00:15:08,045 --> 00:15:14,329
True happiness is when work doesn't feel like work.

93
00:15:14,329 --> 00:15:24,645
"It's when hands dirty with flour are the cleanest hands in the world."

